('111.4.b.3.D',3,'Mia says a ribbon cut into 4 parts is cut into fourths. What must be true for Mia to be right?','["All 4 parts are the same size.", "The parts are all shorter than 4 inches.", "All 4 parts are different sizes.", "The ribbon is red."]'::jsonb,0,'Fourths are 4 equal-sized parts.','original'),
('111.4.b.3.D',2,'Which shape is split into 2 equal parts (halves)?','["A square split into 3 parts", "A circle with a line straight through its center", "A circle with a line near one edge", "A rectangle split into 4 equal parts"]'::jsonb,1,'A line through the center of a circle makes 2 equal parts.','original'),
('111.4.b.3.B',3,'A sandwich is cut into halves. Another identical sandwich is cut into fourths. Which piece is larger?','["It is impossible to tell.", "They are the same size.", "one half", "one fourth"]'::jsonb,2,'Fewer equal parts means each part is larger, so a half is larger than a fourth.','original'),
('111.4.b.3.B',3,'Which statement is true?','["One eighth of a pizza is larger than one fourth of the same pizza.", "One eighth is larger than one half of the same pizza.", "One eighth and one fourth are the same size.", "One eighth of a pizza is smaller than one fourth of the same pizza."]'::jsonb,3,'More parts means smaller parts: eighths are smaller than fourths.','original'),
('111.4.b.6.A',3,'Which situation is multiplication, joining equal groups?','["4 bags with 3 apples in each bag, how many apples in all", "7 apples and 3 more apples", "12 apples shared equally among 4 bags", "12 apples and 4 are eaten"]'::jsonb,0,'Joining equal groups is multiplication.','original'),
('111.4.b.6.B',3,'Which situation is division, splitting a set into equal groups?','["15 grapes and 3 more grapes", "15 grapes are shared equally among 3 friends", "3 friends each have 5 grapes, how many in all", "3 groups of 5 grapes are put in a bowl"]'::jsonb,1,'Sharing a set equally into groups is division.','original'),
